.Dd October 21, 2026
.Dt HEAD 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm head
.Nd display first lines of files
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl n Ar number
.Op Ar file ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
prints the first
.Ar number
lines of a file, if
.Ar number
is not provided,
.Nm
will read the first 10 lines.
.Pp
if
.Ar file ...
is not provided,
.Nm
will read from stdin.
.Pp
if multiple files are provided,
.Nm
will prepend the
.Qq ==> filename <==
header to each read file.
.Pp
the options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl n Ar number
read the first
.Ar number
lines of a file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh AUTHORS
.An juanvel400
